  "locked_findings": [
    "Reranking improves overall Recall@1 from 0.7625 to 0.85 and MRR@5 from 0.8525 to 0.9021.",
    "Reranking lowers overall Recall@5 from 0.975 to 0.9625 and lowers native-PDF MRR@5 from 0.9425 to 0.9333, so it does not pass every non-regression gate.",
    "Table questions are the main candidate-recall gap: Hybrid candidate recall is 0.9 and reranked Recall@5 is 0.8.",
    "The development refusal threshold reduces locked false answers to 5% but falsely refuses 35% of answerable questions.",
    "The hard threshold falsely refuses 50% of scanned-PDF answerable questions; its only no-answer false positive is in the wrong-entity-or-school group.",
    "The locked result must not be used to tune this evaluation cycle; table extraction and refusal modeling require a new development/locked cycle."
  ],
